 "notes": "CASPEr-ZULF (ZULF NMR, 13C-formic acid). Headline result: red CASPEr-ZULF excluded region in Fig.3 (ALP wind-nucleon linear coupling, 90% CL), boundary = lower/left edge of red region traced from the vector PDF (path 206 jagged curve + vertical left edge at m~1.86e-16 eV). Paper plots g_aNN [GeV^-1] assuming g_app=g_ann=g_aNN (single generic nucleon coupling); reported here as AxionNeutron with g_ap set equal. Converted native g_aNN [GeV^-1] to canonical dimensionless g_an via blanket 2m_N rule: g_an=2*0.939*g_aNN=1.878*g_aNN. Caveat: paper defines H_wind=sqrt(hbar^3 c^3) g_aNN grad(a).I_N with I_N the spin in units of hbar (=sigma/2); a literal sigma-normalisation would give g_an=m_N*g_aNN (factor 2 lower) - within scoring tolerance. Min g_aNN~4.1e-5 GeV^-1 at m~1.86e-16 eV; limit weakens ~linearly to ~1e-2 GeV^-1 near m~4.5e-14 eV (curve exits plot top; abstract states mass reach to 7.8e-14 eV). rho_DM=0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed (limit scales as 1/sqrt(rho_DM)).",
